60	English translation\n1\n2026.08.18 | AX Roundtable - Vice President\nThis session was held to organize the recurring document-writing work involved in\nidentifying, proposing, and executing public-sector projects, and to review how\nmuch of that work can be standardized and automated through AX.\nThe discussion emphasized that the goal is not merely to make one individual's work easier. More\nimportantly, the company should establish a system that enables less-experienced staff to prepare\nproposals and project-delivery documents according to the same standards and quality level.\n2. Overview of the End-to-End Public-Sector Project Process\nThe public-sector project workflow explained by the Vice President can be summarized as follows.\n Opportunity discovery and sales -> Support for business plan preparation -> Budget\nproposal development -> Internal approval and decision to proceed -> RFP / statement\n of work preparation -> Proposal preparation -> Presentation materials -> Contract\naward -> Project commencement documents -> Project execution plan -> Weekly and\n monthly reports -> Risk and issue management -> Interim report -> Completion /\n performance report\nDocument structures differ somewhat between central-government projects and local-government\nor municipal projects. For central-government projects, an RFP is generally developed after the\nbusiness plan. For municipal projects, a statement of work is often prepared together with the RFP.\nDuring the early stage of public-sector sales, it is especially important to obtain the business plan\nor participate directly in preparing it. The business plan often contains the most specific description\nof the project purpose, scope, content, and budget.\n3. Core AX Need 1: Automating Public-Sector Project\nDocuments\nCurrent problem\nMany documents must be created at each project stage. Staff repeatedly copy and paste from\nprevious materials and rewrite the documents for every new project.\nThe following documents recur across projects:\n●\nBusiness plan\n●\nProposal\n●\nPresentation materials\n●\nProject commencement documents\n●\nProject execution plan\n●\nWeekly report\n●\nMonthly report\n\nEnglish translation\n2\n●\nRisk management materials\n●\nIssue management materials\n●\nInterim report\n●\nCompletion / performance report\nFor documents such as weekly and monthly reports, whose basic structure is nearly identical each\ntime, the system should automatically insert the relevant period's content into a fixed template\ninstead of requiring the document to be recreated.	[-0.024902344,-0.075683594,-0.0073242188,-0.08984375,0.011230469,-0.048828125,0.033203125,-0.045654297,-0.017700195,-0.020019531,-0.049560547,-0.041259766,0.03149414,-0.008911133,-0.028686523,0.011047363,-0.114746094,0.008117676,-0.06298828,0.0625,-0.055908203,0.016967773,-0.0077819824,-0.020507812,-0.052978516,-0.009460449,0.021118164,0.009216309,0.028686523,-0.03149414,0.04638672,0.0051574707,-0.049316406,0.020629883,0.012634277,-0.0134887695,-0.031982422,-0.0546875,-0.01977539,0.03881836,0.026855469,0.06591797,0.02319336,0.030273438,0.0046081543,-0.06591797,-0.045166016,0.0002708435,0.004272461,0.030273438,-0.0039367676,0.0026245117,0.020874023,0.057861328,-0.036376953,0.037353516,-0.000121593475,-0.04638672,-0.032714844,0.061035156,0.05859375,0.018188477,-0.029663086,-0.009094238,-0.033691406,0.0026245117,0.0154418945,-0.0099487305,0.006286621,-0.0031433105,-0.012329102,-0.0015792847,-0.03149414,0.021972656,-0.0034179688,0.008239746,0.0029754639,0.018310547,0.02331543,-0.042236328,-0.02368164,0.04345703,-0.01574707,0.0004787445,-0.02355957,0.0859375,-0.017700195,0.029296875,-0.016601562,-0.072265625,-0.034179688,0.004486084,0.03125,0.03930664,0.072265625,-0.010681152,0.00062179565,-0.026489258,-0.010437012,0.0043945312,-0.004119873,-0.0024261475,-0.009765625,0.011657715,-0.009521484,0.021362305,-0.02758789,0.005554199,-0.036621094,-0.07080078,-0.00390625,-0.05078125,-0.07080078,0.040771484,-0.005