61	English translation\n2\n●\nRisk management materials\n●\nIssue management materials\n●\nInterim report\n●\nCompletion / performance report\nFor documents such as weekly and monthly reports, whose basic structure is nearly identical each\ntime, the system should automatically insert the relevant period's content into a fixed template\ninstead of requiring the document to be recreated.\nTarget workflow\n Enter core project information -> Determine the current project stage -> Recommend\n required deliverables -> Load company-standard templates -> Insert prior materials\nand project information -> Generate a draft -> Owner reviews and revises -> Generate\n the final document\nThe ideal end state is for a user to make a request such as:\n"Create the documents required for the commencement stage of this\nproject."\nThe AX system would then determine the required deliverables and draft them according to\ncompany standards.\n4. Core AX Need 2: Standardizing Documents and\nDeliverables\nOne of the most important points emphasized by the Vice President was the standardization of both\ninternal and external documents.\nCurrently, writing practices differ by owner, and there is no systematic standard defining which\ndocuments are required at each project stage. This can make it difficult for less-experienced staff\nto carry out the work itself.\nPriority areas for internal standardization\n●\nMandatory deliverables by project stage\n●\nTable of contents for each deliverable\n●\nWriting standards for each document\n●\nCommon proposal sections\n●\nProject management methodology\n●\nProject support methodology\n●\nRisk management approach\n●\nIssue management approach\n●\nReport templates\n●\nCompany-wide expressions and terminology\n\nEnglish translation\n3\nAX can only function properly after these standards are defined. The system should not allow AI to\ncreate documents arbitrarily; it should generate them from company-approved reference\ndocuments and rules.\n5. Core AX Need 3: Templating Common Proposal Sections\nAlthough the technical content of proposals differs by project, many sections are repeated across\nproposals.\n●\nCompany introduction\n●\nGeneral company profile\n●\nProject management\n●\nProject support\n●\nQuality and operations content\n●\nDelivery methodology\nThese sections do not need to be rewritten for every project. They can be maintained as reusable\ncompany-standard content and methodologies. By contrast, technical content and\nrequirement-response sections should be written separately for each project using the RFP.	[-0.009765625,-0.029541016,-0.006439209,-0.10888672,-0.012023926,-0.01977539,0.061523438,-0.06689453,-0.018188477,-0.053466797,-0.026977539,-0.04345703,-0.022338867,-0.0074768066,-0.016845703,0.05078125,-0.091796875,0.022460938,-0.091796875,0.036865234,-0.045410156,-0.008361816,-0.052001953,-0.007659912,-0.026000977,-0.033691406,-0.0005531311,0.056152344,0.008117676,-0.007385254,0.01184082,-0.022338867,-0.03491211,0.006072998,-0.0013580322,-0.012145996,-0.029174805,-0.061523438,-0.025756836,0.020629883,-0.0056762695,0.06689453,0.03564453,0.008361816,-0.012451172,-0.057617188,-0.05053711,-0.0026550293,0.045898438,-0.00022411346,0.025268555,0.03173828,0.02758789,0.0068359375,-0.016479492,0.0053100586,0.007385254,-0.079589844,-0.048583984,0.032226562,0.017333984,-0.044921875,-0.022216797,-0.00793457,-0.012207031,0.01574707,0.026855469,0.0042419434,-0.00038146973,-0.010192871,-0.018920898,-0.016357422,-0.018310547,-0.0033569336,0.0057373047,0.016723633,-0.009887695,0.022705078,0.016113281,0.0390625,-0.030517578,0.008605957,0.007659912,-0.005126953,0.013793945,0.087402344,-0.043701172,0.0030975342,0.0068969727,-0.056396484,-0.016967773,0.004760742,0.008056641,0.036865234,0.064453125,-0.009765625,-0.013122559,-0.013305664,0.005218506,0.016479492,-0.017333984,-0.018554688,0.015075684,0.052734375,0.012756348,0.033691406,-0.041259766,0.0013198853,-0.026733398,-0.05883789,0.0068969727,-0.012634277,-0.066894