63	Proposed operating model\n Register the company-standard glossary -> Upload a draft document -> AI reviews the\nfull document -> Detect nonstandard terminology -> Suggest company-standard terms\n or automatically replace them\nAutomatic replacement should not be applied indiscriminately, because context may require\ndifferent wording. The system should distinguish between review-and-suggestion mode and\nautomatic-conversion mode.\n8. Core AX Need 6: Generating Documents from Internal\nReference Materials\nRather than simply asking an external AI to "write a proposal," the company should maintain\ninternal reference materials in company-managed storage, including:\n●\nStandard templates\n●\nCompany glossary\n●\nPast proposals\n●\nProject execution plans\n●\nProject management methodology\n●\nReport samples\n●\nProject-specific deliverables\n Internal storage -> Store reference documents -> RAG / search -> Retrieve relevant\nstandards -> Generate an AI draft -> Display the reference documents and sources used\nAfter a document is generated, users must be able to identify which reference documents were\nused to create each part of the content.\n9. Core AX Need 7: A System Usable by Less-Experienced\nStaff\nA key direction from the discussion was to build a system that makes the Vice President's\nexperience and working methods available to the entire organization, rather than automating work\nonly for the Vice President personally.\nThrough extensive experience, the Vice President knows:\n\nEnglish translation\n5\n●\nWhich deliverables are needed and when\n●\nWhich table of contents should be used\n●\nHow a project should be managed\n●\nHow a proposal's logic should be structured\nNot every employee has the same experience. Converting that knowledge into rules, templates,\nstandards, and AI agents would make it possible to maintain consistent work quality even when the\nperson responsible changes.\nFor example, once a project is awarded, the system could automatically guide the next steps:\n"Project commencement documents are required."\n"A project execution plan must be prepared."\n"A weekly report template will now be generated."\n10. Automated Collection of Government Projects and\nPolicy Information\nAutomated monitoring of government projects and health-and-welfare information, discussed in the\nprevious AX session, was again raised in connection with the Vice President's work.\nRelevant information is already reviewed daily using AI and other tools, but it should be\naccumulated as a company information asset rather than remaining at the individual level.	[-0.03149414,-0.07763672,-0.007507324,-0.08886719,-0.0234375,-0.03112793,0.04663086,-0.08154297,-0.039794922,-0.03540039,-0.037841797,-0.050048828,-0.0070495605,-0.008056641,-0.03515625,0.016113281,-0.140625,0.03149414,-0.08691406,0.05053711,-0.03173828,0,-0.015075684,-0.0075683594,-0.042236328,-0.025268555,0.007385254,0.047851562,0.0054016113,-0.0146484375,0,-0.011779785,-0.043701172,0.0076293945,0.024658203,-0.012573242,-0.06298828,-0.022949219,-0.022338867,0.011108398,-0.019042969,0.0625,0.063964844,0.030761719,-0.051757812,-0.06689453,-0.025756836,-0.007507324,0.009216309,0.0033569336,-0.011169434,0.007171631,0.0003604889,-0.017822266,-0.037353516,-0.016235352,0.029052734,-0.0390625,-0.04296875,0.057617188,0.036865234,-0.032714844,-0.03515625,0.045898438,-0.025756836,0.038085938,0.022216797,0.06640625,-0.008666992,-0.025024414,-0.024536133,-0.017333984,-0.020996094,-0.0073547363,0.013549805,-0.009033203,0.004272461,0.00793457,0.020507812,0.016357422,-0.022216797,0.025268555,0.051513672,0.0059814453,-0.0087890625,0.056640625,-0.015625,0.025756836,0.029663086,-0.04248047,0.0024719238,0.020874023,0.005126953,0.06689453,0.04663086,-0.010009766,-0.013000488,-0.016357422,0.0008430481,0.003540039,0.008911133,-0.015380859,0.049560547,0.056640625,-0.016357422,0.028686523,-0.0859375,0.0054016113,-0.021240234,-0.045654297,-0.021850586,-0.033447266,-0.025146484,0.05029297,0.0351