64	Automated Collection of Government Projects and\nPolicy Information\nAutomated monitoring of government projects and health-and-welfare information, discussed in the\nprevious AX session, was again raised in connection with the Vice President's work.\nRelevant information is already reviewed daily using AI and other tools, but it should be\naccumulated as a company information asset rather than remaining at the individual level.\n Register relevant websites and keywords -> Search automatically every day -> Select\nmaterials relevant to Ansimjigimi -> Summarize links and key points -> Notify only on\n new materials -> Store internally -> Make the history searchable\nThe key is to build a shared corporate knowledge base instead of ending the process after an\nindividual checks the information.\n11. Need for Image and Diagram Generation\nOne relatively inconvenient part of the Vice President's work is quickly creating proposal images,\nstructural diagrams, and architecture visuals.\nAI is already used extensively for text-based document writing, but the following visual materials\nstill require significant time:\n●\nExplanatory images\n●\nConfiguration diagrams\n●\nArchitecture diagrams\n●\nStructural diagrams\n●\nTables and visual diagrams\n●\nProject concept diagrams\n\nEnglish translation\n6\nThe company should therefore examine whether image and diagram generation can be\nincorporated into the future document-writing agent.\n12. Automated Document Quality Assurance\nAI can already perform basic typo and spelling checks. A company-level AX system should go\nfurther and validate:\n●\nTypos\n●\nSpelling\n●\nGrammar\n●\nCompliance with the company glossary\n●\nConsistent notation and formatting\n●\nConsistency of expressions across documents\n●\nCompliance with the standard table of contents\n●\nMissing mandatory items\nIn the long term, the appropriate model is a Document QA Agent that verifies whether a document\ncomplies with company standards, rather than a simple grammar checker.\n13. The Vice President's View: Internal Standardization\nComes First\nThe Vice President clearly stated that the company should first organize and unify internal work\nbefore automating external services or the Ansimjigimi service itself.\n1\nUnify the documents, terminology, and work standards used internally.\n2\nStandardize externally submitted documents and external-facing materials.\n3\nApply AI automation based on the established standards.\nBecause people currently perform the same work in different ways, automation cannot produce\nconsistent results until common standards are established.\n14.	[0.00075149536,-0.08886719,-0.008911133,-0.095703125,-0.059326172,-0.04272461,0.041748047,-0.048095703,-0.03491211,-0.064453125,-0.032714844,-0.057373047,-0.010986328,-0.009399414,-0.040283203,0.006500244,-0.15820312,0.037597656,-0.060302734,0.03125,-0.051513672,0.018432617,-0.021484375,0.022949219,-0.045410156,-0.037597656,0.013793945,0.07324219,0.025512695,-0.020263672,0.018798828,0.023925781,-0.04296875,0.014404297,0.017578125,-0.014038086,-0.010986328,-0.015319824,-0.017211914,0.032958984,-0.039794922,0.080078125,0.044189453,-0.00088119507,-0.053466797,-0.08203125,-0.025024414,-0.015991211,0.0030975342,-0.0012054443,0.0071411133,0.0030975342,-0.0078125,0.048095703,-0.015319824,0.014282227,0.032958984,-0.037597656,-0.038085938,0.036621094,-0.0064086914,0.010986328,-0.076171875,0.040039062,-0.026000977,0.028564453,0.024414062,0.030883789,-0.030395508,-0.038330078,-0.018798828,-0.015625,-0.033447266,-0.008117676,0.016479492,-0.010131836,0.006958008,0.040283203,0.02722168,0.025268555,-0.0234375,0.025268555,0.032958984,0.0016555786,-0.017211914,0.061279297,-0.01171875,0.01361084,0.007873535,-0.03857422,-0.021972656,0.0027618408,0.02368164,0.0703125,-0.021118164,-0.056152344,-0.018798828,-0.037841797,0.02319336,0.015991211,-0.016479492,0.01965332,0.083496094,0.032958984,-0.05908203,0.025634766,-0.061767578,0.020019531,-0.024414062,-0.03149414,-0.0120