65	1\nUnify the documents, terminology, and work standards used internally.\n2\nStandardize externally submitted documents and external-facing materials.\n3\nApply AI automation based on the established standards.\nBecause people currently perform the same work in different ways, automation cannot produce\nconsistent results until common standards are established.\n14. Priority Initiatives Identified in This Session\nHighest priority - Standardize the public-sector project process and\ndeliverables\nDefine which deliverables are required at each project stage.\nPriority 2 - Build company-standard document templates\nStart with frequently reused documents such as proposals, project execution plans, and weekly and\nmonthly reports.\nPriority 3 - Build a company-standard glossary\nUse it as the standard for all document creation and review.\n\nEnglish translation\n7\nPriority 4 - Build internal storage and RAG, and register reference\ndocuments\nIntegrate past proposals, execution materials, methodologies, and related sources.\nPriority 5 - Document Generation Agent\nGenerate drafts in company formats from project information and an RFP.\nPriority 6 - Document QA Agent\nAutomatically validate terminology, table of contents, typos, and mandatory items.\nPriority 7 - Government project and policy monitoring automation\nConvert individually collected information into a shared corporate information asset.\nMedium to long term - Automated image, diagram, and architecture\ngeneration\nExtend AX to proposal and presentation production.\n15. Follow-up Actions\n1\nCreate an end-to-end public-sector process map. Organize every stage from opportunity\ndiscovery through completion reporting in a single flow.\n2\nList mandatory deliverables by stage. Distinguish mandatory documents, optional documents,\nand internal management documents.\n3\nCollect existing documents. Gather past business plans, proposals, project execution plans, and\nweekly and monthly reports.\n4\nSelect standard templates. Separate project-specific content from common reusable sections.\n5\nDocument the project management methodology. Convert experience-based practices into an\norganizational standard methodology.\n6\nComplete the company-standard glossary. Use it as the standard for all agents and document\nQA.\n7\nConduct a document automation PoC. Start with highly repetitive weekly reports, monthly\nreports, or a project execution plan.	[-0.003479004,-0.06689453,-0.0054016113,-0.10058594,-0.013122559,-0.033935547,0.026367188,-0.05444336,-0.03857422,-0.039794922,-0.049072266,-0.038330078,-0.011474609,-0.0067749023,-0.037841797,-0.0021514893,-0.13574219,0.038330078,-0.09033203,0.05053711,-0.028808594,0.017333984,-0.0065612793,-0.0053100586,-0.041992188,-0.0099487305,-0.0027770996,0.022827148,0.045898438,-0.0059814453,0.005584717,0.012023926,-0.064941406,0.0053710938,-0.017822266,-0.0119018555,-0.011291504,-0.01550293,-0.022827148,0.03149414,-0.0072631836,0.053955078,0.048828125,0.012329102,-0.04663086,-0.072753906,-0.04711914,0.014892578,-0.0012817383,0.029785156,-0.028442383,-0.008300781,0.020996094,0.01574707,-0.028564453,0.029418945,0.025756836,-0.045166016,-0.045654297,0.037353516,0.041748047,-0.005706787,-0.028686523,-0.0019683838,-0.038330078,0.018798828,0.031982422,0.025146484,-0.007019043,-0.009460449,-0.013305664,-0.0134887695,-0.028076172,-0.029907227,0.014404297,0.0028686523,0.009765625,0.00793457,0.012329102,0.020507812,-0.013977051,0.020996094,0.046142578,-0.0061035156,0.008239746,0.07128906,-0.05078125,0.002822876,-0.015319824,-0.063964844,-0.040527344,0.010620117,0.013671875,0.08203125,0.009643555,-0.028808594,-0.013183594,-0.044677734,0.014892578,-0.0040283203,-0.028564453,0.012329102,0.016235352,0.020874023,-0.010131836,0.024414062,-0.034423828,0.0015869141,-0.036132812,-0.055908203,-0.0071105957,-0.017456055,-0.033203125,0.041748047,0.02368164,-0.0703125,-0.056640625,-0.01928711,-0.029174805,-0.051513672,0.023925781,-0.008361816,0.014160156,0.00205993